<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portici</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Portici is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a> at the foot of Vesuvius, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> king Charles built a royal palace there from 1738, close to the newly discovered ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herculaneum">Herculaneum</a>. The railway from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> to Portici, opened on 3 October 1839, was the first in Italy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portici.jpg" alt="Portici" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ferdinando Scala. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reggia_di_Portici1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
